Subject: [PATCH] msm_vidc: keep the Venus firmware loaded

msm_vidc unloads the video core's firmware 15 s after the last session and loads it
again at the next one, into a 5 MB CMA region (venus_mem) that it needs whole. Early
on that works; after a while in use, pages in the region can no longer be moved out
("venus: Failed to allocate relocatable region of size 500000"), and every hardware
codec fails from then on, the camera's video encoder among them. Loaded while the
region is still clean and never unloaded, the firmware never has to be placed again.
An idle core is power-collapsed either way (qcom,sw-power-collapse); unloading only
gives back the region, which is reserved for it anyway.

The delay stays in debugfs (msm_vidc/firmware_unload_delay) as before; only its
default changes. LineageOS 20 used to set it from init, which needed debugfs, its own
SELinux label and a rule for init.
---
--- drivers/media/platform/msm/vidc/msm_vidc_debug.c
+++ drivers/media/platform/msm/vidc/msm_vidc_debug.c
@@ -28,7 +28,11 @@
 int msm_vidc_dec_dcvs_mode = 0x1;
 int msm_vidc_enc_dcvs_mode = 0x1;
 int msm_vidc_sys_idle_indicator = 0x0;
-u32 msm_vidc_firmware_unload_delay = 15000;
+/*
+ * Never unload the firmware: loading it again needs venus_mem whole, which after a
+ * while in use the kernel can no longer free.
+ */
+u32 msm_vidc_firmware_unload_delay = UINT_MAX;
 int msm_vidc_thermal_mitigation_disabled = 0x0;
 
 struct debug_buffer {
